# ---------- DEVELOPMENT DATABASE ----------
# test.db (database.py's DB_NAME) is local development scratch data, deliberately NOT
# version-controlled: it is a ~23 MB SQLite file that changed on almost every commit, and
# since SQLite doesn't delta-compress, git stored a full fresh copy each time. That is what
# grew .git to 512 MB and made pushes to GitHub time out.
# audit_app.db / data.db / database.db are dead leftovers from earlier naming.
*.db

# SQLite writes these sidecar files alongside the database while it is open.
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Automatic pre-migration backups, created at runtime by database.py's own
# shutil.copy2(DB_NAME, f"{DB_NAME}.bak-premigrate-...") calls — so new ones appear on their
# own whenever a schema upgrade runs. Never useful to commit.
*.bak
*.db.bak*

# ---------- UPLOADED CLIENT FILES ----------
# Real client spreadsheets saved by import_export.py's /api/import-excel endpoint. The folder
# is recreated automatically on first upload (os.makedirs(upload_dir, exist_ok=True)), so
# ignoring it wholesale is safe — nothing needs a .gitkeep placeholder.
uploads/

# ---------- PYTHON RUNTIME ARTEFACTS ----------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
venv/

# ---------- LOGS ----------
uvicorn_err.log
uvicorn_out.log
*.log

# ---------- LOCAL SECRETS ----------
# Holds the real Supabase DATABASE_URL (Phase 2 of the Supabase/Render migration)
# - never committed. See .env.example for the documented, safe-to-share shape.
.env
